      {q:"In an L-cut, the audio of the current clip…",options:["Cuts off exactly with the visual","Continues even after the next visual begins","Is replaced by music","Speeds up"],answer:1,explain:"L-cut = current audio carries into the next visual for a cinematic feel."},
      {q:"The technique that makes jump cuts seamless is called…",options:["Split the difference","Cut the Head and Keep the Tail","Match on action","Freeze and hold"],answer:1,explain:"Remove the head of the next line up to the audio; keep a bit of the previous line's tail."},
