  { num:"4", color:"#F472B6", title:"AI Voiceovers",
    subtitle:"Cloning, remixing, fixing, and grounding a voice in a believable environment.",
    lesson:
`Great voiceovers are built in **Eleven Labs** and then blended into their environment with subtle sound — a street selfie video shouldn't sound like a clean studio recording.

## First steps
- Read the script and watch the reference video.
- Copy the script into **Eleven Labs** (the AI voice tool).
- Remove any unnecessary "hooks + body" text early, so there's less to edit later.
- Use **ALL CAPS** to emphasize words in the voiceover (e.g. NEVER, HOME).
- Proofread for missing punctuation or grammar errors.

## Cloning a voice
Start with a clear voice sample. Use **Voice Isolator** to strip out music or unwanted sounds if needed — but if it's **just light background noise, leave it in**, because that bit of noise helps the cloned voice sound natural. You can also use **vocalremover.org/splitter-ai** to separate the voice from the instruments. Generate the voiceover with the **Eleven Multilingual v2** model.
- If takes sound flat, add **Voice Tags** like [calm], [excited], [angry]. You can draft them with ChatGPT, but always read aloud and adjust yourself.
- Prefer cloning the voice from the **inspiration video** — it's already tested.

## Remixing (accent, age, emotion, gender)
Use **Voice Remixing** and set Prompt Strength: **Low** (clarity/tone/speed), **Medium** (accent/age), **High** (emotion), **Max** (gender).

## Fixing words & speed
Use **Eleven Labs Studio → Transcribe & Edit Speech** to swap a brand name or fix a line seamlessly — it keeps the original tone and pacing, and adjusts speed without changing pitch.

## Realism, distance & depth
Match ambience to the scene (a low car-interior hum, a small-room reverb). To make a voice feel far from the camera, **reduce the high frequencies with a low-pass filter** for a muffled tone, add a touch of reverb, and drop the loudness a little.

## Music
Add music last, matched to mood: **dark / suspenseful for conspiracy or "Big Pharma" ads**, soft/chill/upbeat for UGC. Keep it low enough that the voice stays clear.

To find the exact track from the inspiration video: isolate the audio (Voice Isolator or vocalremover.org), turn up the isolated music/instruments, then identify it with Google's "search a song" feature or Shazam.`,
    questions:[
      {q:"When generating a voiceover from your cloned voice, which model should you always select?",options:["Eleven Multilingual v2","An English-only model","Voice Isolator","Voice Changer"],answer:0,explain:"Generate speech from the clone with the Eleven Multilingual v2 model."},
      {q:"Every generated take sounds flat and monotone. What's the recommended fix?",options:["Add Voice Tags like [calm], [excited], [angry] to the script","Re-record the sample louder","Max out the Stability slider","Switch to a different voice"],answer:0,explain:"Voice Tags add emotion and phonetic variation — draft with ChatGPT, but read aloud and adjust yourself."},
